What the real run showed. The null clause applied: the resolver is fine and I didn't touch its logic. I ran the extractor's own functions over the real audit-log data (10 sessions in the window, 13 task commits). All 6 unchecked sessions are clone-boundary refusals. The clone's oldest commit is 2026-09-28 22:06:25, and each of those 6 windows opens earlier than that. The task expected about 1 unchecked session, but that estimate left out the shallow clone: fetch --depth 50 keeps only about a day of history, which is less than the ~10-session window. There was also a seventh unchecked session the old line never showed at all: the oldest session read (day-211-20260927T235245Z), which has no earlier session to open its window.

